      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add disableBoundaryAwareCache compat option for prefix-matching prompt cache providers",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where DeepSeek and Xiaomi OpenAI-compatible users could lose provider prompt-cache hits after the 6.x boundary-aware cache split put per-turn dynamic context into the system prompt.\n\nCloses #94518\n\nRelated: #91018, #90583\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nDeepSeek/Xiaomi use prefix-matching cache behavior, so their stable system prefix needs to remain byte-stable across turns. This PR adds `compat.disableBoundaryAwareCache`, defaults it on for those providers, keeps only the stable prefix in the system message, and moves the dynamic suffix into the latest user turn so older conversation history stays reusable.\n\nOperators can opt back into normal boundary-aware behavior with `compat: { disableBoundaryAwareCache: false }`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nDeepSeek and Xiaomi users should keep the stable system prompt and prior conversation history cacheable across multi-turn requests instead of invalidating the reusable prefix with each dynamic suffix update.\n\n## Evidence\n\nFocused tests:\n\n```bash\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/llm/providers/openai-completions.test.ts\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests  34 passed (34)\n```\n\n```bash\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/openai-transport-stream.test.ts\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests  287 passed (287)\n```\n\nNon-test production request-building proof:\n\n```bash\n$ node --import tsx E:\\Projects\\auto-pr\\workspace\\openclaw\\outputs\\issue-94518\\request-shape-proof.mts\n{\n  \"model\": \"deepseek-v4-pro\",\n  \"messages\": [\n    { \"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"Stable prefix\" },\n    { \"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Historical request\" },\n    { \"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"Historical answer\" },\n    { \"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Project Context\\n\\nCurrent request\" }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nLive DeepSeek cache proof:\n\n```bash\n$ node --import tsx E:\\Projects\\auto-pr\\workspace\\openclaw\\outputs\\issue-94518\\deepseek-live-payloads.mts\n\"model\": \"deepseek-v4-flash\"\n\"role\": \"system\", \"hasStablePrefix\": true, \"hasDynamicSuffix\": false\n\"role\": \"user\", \"hasHistoricalUser\": true, \"hasDynamicSuffix\": false\n\"role\": \"assistant\"\n\"role\": \"user\", \"hasCurrentRequest\": true, \"hasDynamicSuffix\": true\n```\n\n```bash\n$ Invoke-RestMethod ... https://api.deepseek.com/v1/chat/completions\n[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"first\",\n    \"model\": \"deepseek-v4-flash\",\n    \"prompt_tokens\": 1987,\n    \"completion_tokens\": 216,\n    \"total_tokens\": 2203,\n    \"prompt_cache_hit_tokens\": 1920,\n    \"prompt_cache_miss_tokens\": 67\n  },\n  {\n    \"label\": \"second\",\n    \"model\": \"deepseek-v4-flash\",\n    \"prompt_tokens\": 1987,\n    \"completion_tokens\": 209,\n    \"total_tokens\": 2196,\n    \"prompt_cache_hit_tokens\": 1920,\n    \"prompt_cache_miss_tokens\": 67\n  }\n]\n```\n\nThe live proof used `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` from the local environment. The key was not printed, saved in payload files, or written to the repository.\n\nAI-assisted: built with Codex\n",
        "branch": "fix/deepseek-boundary-aware-cache-94518",
